"], ["**Mother India**", "First Indian Oscar nomination (1958)"], ["**Boong**", "First Indian BAFTA win in Children's & Family Film"], ["**Wagner Moura**", "First Brazilian Golden Globe Best Actor (Drama)"], ["**Amy Poehler**", "First Golden Globe for Best Podcast"], ["**Paul Thomas Anderson**", "First BAFTA for Best Director"], ["**Netaji**", "First to call Gandhi 'Father of the Nation' (6 July 1944)"]]}]}
{"h": "2296ccd32321", "b": [{"k": "h", "x": "The ladder"}, {"k": "t", "h": ["Award", "Rank", "Given for"], "r": [["Bharat Ratna", "1st – highest civilian award", "Exceptional service of the highest order"], ["Padma Vibhushan", "2nd", "Exceptional and distinguished service"], ["Padma Bhushan", "3rd", "Distinguished service of a high order"], ["Padma Shri", "4th", "Distinguished service in any field"]]}, {"k": "t", "h": ["Fact", "Key detail"], "r": [["Instituted", "**1954**"], ["Announced / conferred", "Padma lists announced on **Republic Day**; conferred by the **President** at **Rashtrapati Bhavan** (March–April)"], ["Nature", "Bharat Ratna is a civilian award (the **Param Vir Chakra** is the military gallantry award); the Nobel is not Indian"], ["**Article 18(1)**", "No titles except **military and academic distinctions**"], ["**Balaji Raghavan case (1996)**", "Padma awards are **not titles under Article 18**; not to be used as prefix or suffix"], ["Count", "**2009 – 93 Padma Shri**"]]}, {"k": "h", "x": "Bharat Ratna – firsts and order"}, {"k": "t", "h": ["Fact", "Person", "Year"], "r": [["First woman", "**Indira Gandhi**", "1971"], ["Naturalised Indian", "Mother Teresa", "1980"], ["First non-Indian (foreigner)", "**Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan**", "1987"], ["Second foreigner", "**Nelson Mandela**", "1990"], ["Industrialist + film-maker", "**J.R.D. Tata**, **Satyajit Ray**", "1992"], ["Scientist-President", "A.P.J. Abdul Kalam", "1997"], ["First singer / musician", "**M.S. Subbulakshmi** (also C. Subramaniam)", "1998"], ["Economist", "Amartya Sen", "1999"], ["Singer", "Lata Mangeshkar", "2001"], ["Hindustani vocalist", "**Pt. Bhimsen Joshi** (announced Nov 2008)", "2009"], ["Posthumous singer", "**Bhupen Hazarika** (with Pranab Mukherjee, Nanaji Deshmukh)", "2019"], ["Latest list", "Five awardees incl. **P.V. Narasimha Rao**", "2024"]]}, {"k": "b", "x": "Order: **Kalam 1997 → Subbulakshmi 1998 → Sen 1999 → Lata 2001**."}, {"k": "b", "x": "**Raj Kapoor** got the Dadasahe